<title>BELGIUM: Belgian bankruptcies rose 6.6 pct in November.</title>
<headline>Belgian bankruptcies rose 6.6 pct in November.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Company bankruptcies in Belgium rose by 6.6 percent to 681 in November compared with November 1995, Belgian trade and company data group Infotrade said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>In the first 11 months of 1996 a record total of 6,799 companies went bankrupt, up 5.3 percent from 6,458 in the same 1995 period.</p>
<p>Infotrade said it expected more than 600 extra bankruptcies in December, taking the annual total to a record high of around 7,400 against 7,022 in 1995.</p>
